Where he studied, what food he likes.

261
00:19:40,770 --> 00:19:42,270
Hobbies.

262
00:19:44,670 --> 00:19:47,130
So what does Star like?

263
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,870
You wanna know, huh? Trade me the next plan for it.

264
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,600
Fine, don't tell me then.

265
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,530
You really think you can bargain with me?

266
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:19,500
Go change out of that kit.

267
00:20:21,230 --> 00:20:24,670
Standing around posing like that. Such a drama queen.

268
00:20:29,470 --> 00:20:31,830
"Fuen, I'm not trying to rush you for an answer,"

269
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:33,930
"but I've been thinking — I shouldn't have asked for your help at all."

270
00:20:33,930 --> 00:20:35,930
"Did I put you in a difficult position?"

271
00:20:48,370 --> 00:20:50,370
"Not at all, Star."

272
00:20:50,370 --> 00:20:53,070
"I'm still working on a way for you."

273
00:20:53,070 --> 00:20:54,670
"Really?"

274
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:56,330
"I'm so glad you're helping me."

275
00:20:56,330 --> 00:20:57,770
"Thank you so much."

276
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:03,100
Hey, you still haven't changed?

277
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:04,400
Go change already.

278
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:06,530
What are you posing here for?

279
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:31,100
Hey, why haven't you changed? Why aren't you going home?

280
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:33,270
You sent me off to change all by myself.

281
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:42,300
Bug off! I wanna wear this kit. It looks cool.

282
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:46,000
Football fanboy. Thapfah lover.

283
00:21:47,570 --> 00:21:48,830
Sit.

284
00:21:50,430 --> 00:21:53,030
You want a new plan, right?

285
00:21:53,930 --> 00:21:57,030
Try asking me nicely.

286
00:21:57,930 --> 00:21:59,670
Sweeter than that.

287
00:22:02,070 --> 00:22:04,370
I... want it.

288
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:09,830
Again. Ask sweetly.

289
00:22:10,870 --> 00:22:12,930
I want it, please.

290
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:16,300
Ugh, I'm done playing with you.

291
00:22:16,970 --> 00:22:20,930
Hey. Say, hypothetically, I wanna win someone over.

292
00:22:22,130 --> 00:22:22,830
Mm-hmm.

293
00:22:22,830 --> 00:22:24,370
I'd have to go through their friends, right?

294
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:34,030
Depends. It's about how much that person values their friends.

295
00:22:34,470 --> 00:22:36,470
Why are you asking?

296
00:22:37,470 --> 00:22:43,800
Just curious. Everyone I see going after someone goes through the friends.

297
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:53,000
And if that person isn't interested in us, but we want them to be —

298
00:22:54,770 --> 00:22:56,330
what do we do?

299
00:22:58,370 --> 00:23:02,270
Hey, Fuen, why are you trying this hard?

300
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:07,470
I think if he's gonna like you, he'd like you for who you are.

301
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:19,600
Come on, he doesn't know me the way you know me.

302
00:23:20,630 --> 00:23:25,400
Okay, let me ask again. Hypothetically.

303
00:23:28,570 --> 00:23:30,070
Say it's you and me.

304
00:23:30,930 --> 00:23:33,970
Say I'd liked you for a long time,

305
00:23:39,170 --> 00:23:40,900
and I wanted to win you over.

306
00:23:41,770 --> 00:23:43,270
I want you to notice me,

307
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:46,300
and I want you to come to me.

308
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:53,800
What would work best on you?

309
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:11,470
Same answer. Don't do anything. Just be yourself.

310
00:24:12,030 --> 00:24:13,430
Are you messing with me?

311
00:24:15,230 --> 00:24:20,070
Okay, then what do I do if I want to get to know you?

312
00:24:21,170 --> 00:24:25,500
Just bring yourself close to me. That's all.

313
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,800
Because if I like you,

314
00:24:36,930 --> 00:24:38,800
I'll do the chasing myself.

315
00:24:53,730 --> 00:25:02,200
Oh. So your new plan is to bring myself close to him,

316
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:04,500
and just be myself.

317
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:07,130
That's so deep.

318
00:25:07,830 --> 00:25:10,170
So damn deep. Bleh!

319
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:13,230
Talking to you is boring. / Hey.

320
00:25:13,370 --> 00:25:14,670
Dumbass.

321
00:25:14,670 --> 00:25:16,170
So hard to get through to you.

322
00:25:17,770 --> 00:25:18,870
I already changed.

323
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:26,000
Huh? Didn't you say you liked this kit?

324
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,700
I don't like Aof's kit.

325
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,200
I don't like dumbasses.

326
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:31,430
Aof isn't even here and he still gets it.

327
00:25:36,970 --> 00:25:42,400
You won't tell me? Won't tell. Ugh, won't tell, won't tell. I'm never telling.

328
00:25:45,100 --> 00:25:49,300
Hey, have you guys seen someone named Chemi in this class?

329
00:25:49,300 --> 00:25:52,130
Oh, Physics's little brother? / Mm-hmm.

330
00:25:52,130 --> 00:25:54,330
Oh, I saw him sitting at the football field.

331
00:25:54,330 --> 00:25:56,500
Yes, the whole group is there.

332
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:58,870
Oh, oh, tell me.

333
00:25:58,870 --> 00:26:00,600
You're hopeless.

334
00:26:17,070 --> 00:26:19,500
"I tricked the answer out of Physics for you."

335
00:26:21,670 --> 00:26:23,100
"He said if you want him to notice you,"

336
00:26:23,100 --> 00:26:26,130
"just bring yourself close enough for him to chase, and be yourself."

337
00:26:26,130 --> 00:26:27,670
"Sorry. This is all the help I can give."

338
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:30,400
Time.

339
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:40,570
So Physics likes to be the one doing the chasing.

340
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:44,500
But bringing myself close enough for him to chase, that's...

341
00:26:49,430 --> 00:26:53,430
But I think if we get ourselves close to Physics,

342
00:26:54,130 --> 00:26:59,700
and stay in his line of sight, we'd get to talk sometimes.

343
00:27:01,630 --> 00:27:03,130
Not bad, not bad.

344
00:27:03,130 --> 00:27:05,200
Let me see what you two talked about.

345
00:27:05,570 --> 00:27:06,900
That's enough. / Hey.

346
00:27:22,930 --> 00:27:25,230
Here's your kit. Give one to your friend.

347
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:28,070
All right, staff, listen up.

348
00:27:28,070 --> 00:27:31,870
Our team normally has 7 starters and 3 substitutes.

349
00:27:31,870 --> 00:27:34,630
We usually prepare 2 bottles of water per person,

350
00:27:34,630 --> 00:27:37,600
plus 10 spare bottles and 1 cold towel each.

351
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,800
Are you listening?

352
00:27:40,130 --> 00:27:41,600
Yes, sir. / We're listening.

353
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:42,500
Listening, sir.

354
00:27:42,630 --> 00:27:45,470
So while everyone's training,

355
00:27:45,470 --> 00:27:47,970
is there anything else we need to do?

356
00:27:47,970 --> 00:27:51,530
Usually you take the towels to wash and check the stock.

357
00:27:51,530 --> 00:27:55,570
And go ask each player if they need anything else.

358
00:27:55,570 --> 00:27:59,470
But honestly you don't have to — they all come well prepared.

359
00:27:59,470 --> 00:28:03,200
Oh, and some of them hide it when they're hurt. Keep an eye out.

360
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:06,700
Before we came, did you do all of this alone? / Yes.

361
00:28:06,700 --> 00:28:08,200
Otherwise I wouldn't be here teaching you.

362
00:28:08,200 --> 00:28:10,030
Pass it properly. Good.

363
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:16,230
So during training, don't we wait for the team captain?

364
00:28:16,230 --> 00:28:18,200
I haven't seen Aof at all.

365
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:19,170
There he is.

366
00:28:31,930 --> 00:28:33,630
What are you doing? / Sorry, sorry, sorry.

367
00:28:33,630 --> 00:28:35,500
Let's train, everyone, come on.

368
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:43,100
I'll leave them with you. I've got other things to do.

369
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,300
Yes, sir.

370
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,530
Eyes on the ball.

371
00:28:56,300 --> 00:28:58,230
Not your eyes one way and your feet the other.

372
00:29:02,330 --> 00:29:04,670
Aof, the goal is right there.

373
00:29:04,670 --> 00:29:06,470
Yes, Coach. Sorry, Coach.

374
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:19,500
One bottle, please.

375
00:30:28,070 --> 00:30:29,370
Chemi.

376
00:30:30,470 --> 00:30:33,200
Don't rush off after training today.

377
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:35,900
There's something I want to talk to you about.

378
00:30:36,900 --> 00:30:38,170
Okay.

379
00:30:39,770 --> 00:30:41,100
Gather up, gather up.

380
00:30:44,870 --> 00:30:49,000
We've got a friendly match coming up against Suan Mali School.

381
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,200
Yes, Coach.

382
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:52,530
I want all of you to take this seriously.

383
00:30:52,530 --> 00:30:54,670
Judging by today's training form,

384
00:30:55,970 --> 00:30:57,630
we'd be better off not playing at all.

385
00:30:57,630 --> 00:30:58,930
Come on, Coach.

386
00:30:59,370 --> 00:31:01,200
Coach, it's only the first day of term.

387
00:31:01,530 --> 00:31:02,900
Your passing,

388
00:31:02,900 --> 00:31:05,230
your chemistry — it's all gone.

389
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:08,470
You need to get it back as fast as possible. Understood?

390
00:31:08,470 --> 00:31:09,770
Yes, Coach.

391
00:31:09,770 --> 00:31:10,900
Any questions?

392
00:31:11,530 --> 00:31:12,830
Coach. / Go ahead.

393
00:31:12,830 --> 00:31:16,000
Who's Suan Mali's captain this time?

394
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:18,530
Hmm, sounds like they're still deciding.

395
00:31:19,100 --> 00:31:22,870
And this year, you're team captain.

396
00:31:24,700 --> 00:31:26,170
Yes, Coach!

397
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:31,970
You are not to let this team down. Understood?

398
00:31:31,970 --> 00:31:32,970
Yes, sir.

399
00:31:32,970 --> 00:31:35,900
And let Thanop help you out.

400
00:31:35,900 --> 00:31:38,300
Talk things through. Don't bite each other's heads off.

401
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:41,130
Understood? / Yes, Coach.

402
00:31:41,730 --> 00:31:45,800
And this year we've got M.4 juniors signing up as staff.

403
00:31:46,470 --> 00:31:48,600
Let's give them a hand.

404
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:58,100
Don't you dare haze them. Especially you, Aof.

405
00:31:58,100 --> 00:31:59,170
Yes, Coach.

406
00:31:59,170 --> 00:32:00,830
All right. Go home.

407
00:32:00,830 --> 00:32:03,070
Hey. / Thanks a lot.

408
00:32:27,700 --> 00:32:30,430
Huh, Physics isn't here.

409
00:32:30,430 --> 00:32:31,800
Nobody's here.

410
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:40,000
Fuen, has Physics gone home already?

411
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:42,900
I just stopped by the classroom.

412
00:32:44,530 --> 00:32:46,170
What do we do, Time?

413
00:32:46,170 --> 00:32:48,300
I dunno. Just leave it on the desk?

414
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:51,370
Damn it, I really am forgetful.

415
00:32:51,370 --> 00:32:53,300
Where are you going? / Time, hide.

416
00:32:53,300 --> 00:32:54,830
Hide, hide. Why? / Hide!

417
00:32:56,330 --> 00:32:58,370
There it is. I really did forget it.

418
00:32:58,370 --> 00:33:01,230
Got everything? You're not forgetting anything else?

419
00:33:01,630 --> 00:33:03,300
Let's go, so we can get home.

420
00:33:03,300 --> 00:33:05,530
"Fuen, has Physics gone home already?"

421
00:33:05,530 --> 00:33:07,230
"I just stopped by the classroom."

422
00:33:07,230 --> 00:33:08,900
What else are you looking for?

423
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:17,400
Nothing, man. Let's go, let's hurry home. / Really?

424
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:20,300
Yeah, eyes forward, straight ahead. Go home, go home.

425
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:28,570
Why are we hiding? We didn't do anything wrong.

426
00:33:29,130 --> 00:33:34,430
I don't know. I'm just not ready to face him yet.

427
00:33:37,070 --> 00:33:39,070
Then we'll give it to him another time.

428
00:33:39,670 --> 00:33:43,130
Come on, it's just snacks. How hard can it be?

429
00:33:43,130 --> 00:33:44,930
Time won't be us. Time doesn't get it.

430
00:33:50,600 --> 00:33:52,070
Physics...

431
00:33:53,270 --> 00:33:55,070
What are you doing here?

432
00:33:55,070 --> 00:33:58,000
Um, I'm on the student council. Just checking the classroom.

433
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:00,970
Sorry on my friend's behalf. We'll be going now.

434
00:34:30,570 --> 00:34:31,730
Chemi. / Ah!

435
00:34:32,870 --> 00:34:33,969
Aof.

436
00:34:36,870 --> 00:34:39,230
Sorry. I didn't think you'd actually be startled.

437
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:43,570
Come on, let's go home.

438
00:34:44,830 --> 00:34:45,900
I'll take you.

439
00:34:46,730 --> 00:34:48,600
Oh, I have a question.

440
00:34:49,770 --> 00:34:52,170
Why did you join the football club?

441
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:56,070
Don't you not like sports?

442
00:35:03,100 --> 00:35:06,900
Oh... right. Yes.

443
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:11,070
My friends are all in this club.

444
00:35:11,070 --> 00:35:13,870
If I went off on my own, I'd be lonely.

445
00:35:14,370 --> 00:35:17,400
Mm, okay.

446
00:35:17,800 --> 00:35:21,070
But staff work is heavy, you know.

447
00:35:21,900 --> 00:35:24,100
At first it may not seem like much,

448
00:35:24,100 --> 00:35:26,530
but once the matches get close, or during training camp,

449
00:35:26,530 --> 00:35:28,470
there's barely any free time.

450
00:35:29,870 --> 00:35:32,530
I think you'd be better off in a club you actually like.

451
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:33,830
Less tiring too.

452
00:35:40,070 --> 00:35:43,100
If I can't handle it, I'll file a transfer then.

453
00:35:44,430 --> 00:35:47,070
But today I actually had fun.

454
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:00,830
Come on, let's go home.

455
00:36:18,430 --> 00:36:20,870
All done. Chemi, give it a try.

456
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:22,970
Thank you.

457
00:36:34,200 --> 00:36:35,770
Thank you, Aof.

458
00:36:36,870 --> 00:36:42,970
Hey, Aof, I saw that my brother likes Fuen.

459
00:36:42,970 --> 00:36:45,630
So they'll end up together, right?

460
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:48,730
Probably, but who knows when Fuen will realize it.

461
00:36:50,130 --> 00:36:52,700
And what if I want a boyfriend too?

462
00:36:52,700 --> 00:36:54,930
Do I have to wait until secondary school?

463
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:04,200
How about this — if you don't have anyone by then,

464
00:37:04,200 --> 00:37:06,230
I'll be your first boyfriend myself.

465
00:37:09,100 --> 00:37:11,370
Hey, Aof, what are you doing? It's dirty.

466
00:37:11,370 --> 00:37:13,000
So we'd match.

467
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:15,500
Then promise me, Aof.

468
00:37:22,030 --> 00:37:24,130
Get home safe. Your ride's here.

469
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,670
Thank you.

470
00:37:30,870 --> 00:37:32,300
Get home safe.

471
00:37:35,130 --> 00:37:39,630
Aof, back then you told me...

472
00:37:40,570 --> 00:37:42,230
once I got to upper secondary,

473
00:37:43,670 --> 00:37:44,730
you'd...

474
00:37:47,370 --> 00:37:51,900
♪ There's something in my heart I can't explain ♪

475
00:37:51,900 --> 00:37:56,230
♪ Still searching for someone to tell me ♪

476
00:37:56,230 --> 00:37:59,770
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

477
00:37:59,770 --> 00:38:02,130
♪ I never find what I'm looking for ♪

478
00:38:02,130 --> 00:38:05,970
♪ Why does my heart still feel so empty? ♪

479
00:38:05,970 --> 00:38:09,870
♪ I want to think it through, to find an answer ♪

480
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:14,400
♪ To these feelings I can't read ♪

481
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:17,970
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

482
00:38:17,970 --> 00:38:24,500
♪ I still want to know — is there someone who can help me? ♪

483
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:41,200
Fuen.

484
00:38:42,030 --> 00:38:44,770
What's wrong with you? Something you're not telling me?

485
00:38:44,770 --> 00:38:48,430
Nothing's wrong. You're the nosy one here.

486
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:51,770
Ugh...

487
00:39:00,270 --> 00:39:03,730
Ever since you got to my place you haven't said a word.

488
00:39:03,730 --> 00:39:05,530
How am I not supposed to wonder?

489
00:39:06,700 --> 00:39:12,270
I've just been overthinking about Star. You know how much I like him.

490
00:39:12,270 --> 00:39:16,430
But... I think I'm getting my heart broken.

491
00:39:22,330 --> 00:39:25,830
Oh, come on, man. That's nothing.

492
00:39:25,830 --> 00:39:29,630
You know what? Nobody ever died of a broken heart.

493
00:39:29,630 --> 00:39:31,870
I think you should be glad, actually.

494
00:39:31,870 --> 00:39:35,070
Because if that day really comes, you've still got me.

495
00:39:37,670 --> 00:39:41,830
Yeah, right. Once you get a boyfriend you'll ditch me.

496
00:39:47,670 --> 00:39:49,270
I like the look on your face right now.

497
00:39:51,730 --> 00:39:53,130
Are you making fun of me?

498
00:39:53,130 --> 00:39:55,130
I may not be as handsome as you,

499
00:39:55,700 --> 00:39:57,430
but you don't get to bully me.

500
00:40:02,570 --> 00:40:03,870
I really do like it.

501
00:40:10,900 --> 00:40:12,570
Take a picture with me.

502
00:40:22,270 --> 00:40:26,030
What the hell? You make fun of me and then want a photo—

503
00:40:28,530 --> 00:40:30,700
Ow. Hey, Fuen.

504
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:35,400
I don't know why you're stressing so much over Star.

505
00:40:36,630 --> 00:40:40,000
In the end, if he really gets to know you

506
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,800
and he still doesn't like you,

507
00:40:41,800 --> 00:40:43,630
you should let it go.

508
00:40:46,100 --> 00:40:49,600
Because to me, you as you are right now

509
00:40:50,570 --> 00:40:51,900
is already the best there is.

510
00:41:09,130 --> 00:41:13,130
Physics, isn't that what you say when you're praising a dog?

511
00:41:20,600 --> 00:41:22,170
Bow-wow...

512
00:41:23,100 --> 00:41:24,770
You, Fuen —

513
00:41:25,630 --> 00:41:29,670
sometimes it'd be nice if you got a little smarter.

514
00:41:31,630 --> 00:41:34,570
Bow-wow. / Bow-wow, bow-wow.

515
00:41:36,900 --> 00:41:38,930
Bow-wow.

516
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:43,170
Stand at ease.

517
00:41:44,400 --> 00:41:48,470
Good morning, third-year cadets.

518
00:41:48,470 --> 00:41:52,670
Today we'll be training in infantry tactics.

519
00:41:52,670 --> 00:41:55,330
Specifically, movement on the battlefield.

520
00:41:56,630 --> 00:41:59,470
Next, once you're all set,

521
00:41:59,470 --> 00:42:03,330
we'll begin the tactics training session.

522
00:42:03,330 --> 00:42:06,070
I'll call attention, then right face.

523
00:42:06,070 --> 00:42:11,900
Cadets — attention! Right face!

524
00:42:12,930 --> 00:42:15,700
Louder. Acknowledged. / Acknowledged!

525
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:17,730
Again. Acknowledged. / Acknowledged!

526
00:42:21,300 --> 00:42:24,530
Good morning, third-year cadets.

527
00:42:24,530 --> 00:42:27,830
This morning's session covers the assault —

528
00:42:27,830 --> 00:42:31,100
movement across the field: bounding rush, crawl, prone.

529
00:42:31,470 --> 00:42:33,670
Every one of you will practise it.

530
00:42:33,670 --> 00:42:37,400
Let me stress safety. Everyone stay alert.

531
00:42:37,870 --> 00:42:42,530
First, weapon handling — how to hold it safely without hitting a comrade.

532
00:42:42,530 --> 00:42:45,830
Because in practice you'll have comrades right beside you.

533
00:42:46,370 --> 00:42:50,000
Let's see a demonstration from the platoon leader on weapon handling.

534
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:51,630
Platoon leader, please. / Yes, sir.

535
00:42:54,370 --> 00:42:56,230
Say you're at attention.

536
00:42:58,900 --> 00:42:59,870
Order arms.

537
00:42:59,870 --> 00:43:03,770
Your right hand grips it, like this.

538
00:43:05,470 --> 00:43:08,930
And when you move, bring the weapon up.

539
00:43:11,800 --> 00:43:13,400
Everyone, on your feet.

540
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:18,230
All right, head over to the training ground. Go ahead.

541
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:28,230
The assault is divided into three phases.

542
00:43:28,230 --> 00:43:34,400
We move in bounds, by fire team, or by rifle squad.

543
00:43:34,400 --> 00:43:37,030
Moving toward the enemy, we reduce the unit size —

544
00:43:37,500 --> 00:43:42,330
from squad, down to fire team, then by pairs, then one man at a time.

545
00:43:42,330 --> 00:43:47,870
And there'll be a simulated obstacle during our movement: barbed wire ahead.

546
00:43:47,870 --> 00:43:51,500
Let me stress — when you cross the barbed wire obstacle,

547
00:43:51,500 --> 00:43:53,870
use your weapon to push it. Push.

548
00:43:53,870 --> 00:43:56,430
Grip the weapon like this to push the wire. Don't wrap your hand around it.

549
00:43:56,430 --> 00:43:58,700
If you wrap your hand around it, your hand will scrape the barbed wire.

550
00:43:59,570 --> 00:44:01,530
Knees low, use your back to move.

551
00:44:01,530 --> 00:44:05,270
Grip it like this and push. When you're ready,

552
00:44:05,270 --> 00:44:09,270
we'll begin. First group — positions!

553
00:44:14,570 --> 00:44:16,800
Sit down. Sit, sit right down.

554
00:44:20,430 --> 00:44:21,500
First squad!

555
00:44:24,770 --> 00:44:26,730
First squad! / First squad!

556
00:44:26,730 --> 00:44:28,870
Move forward! / Move forward!

557
00:44:28,870 --> 00:44:31,330
By bounding rush! / By bounding rush!

558
00:44:31,330 --> 00:44:33,230
Five metres! / Five metres!

559
00:44:33,230 --> 00:44:35,000
Whole squad! / Whole squad!

560
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:36,070
Go!

561
00:45:47,300 --> 00:45:51,070
All right, I'll give you a 10-minute break. Ten minutes.

562
00:45:51,870 --> 00:45:53,700
Dismissed. / Yes, sir.

563
00:46:04,170 --> 00:46:06,770
I'm starving. Let's hit the shop. / Yeah.

564
00:46:06,770 --> 00:46:08,270
Hold my rifle for me.

565
00:46:12,230 --> 00:46:13,130
Hey.

566
00:46:14,430 --> 00:46:16,230
He only gave us 10 minutes.

567
00:46:16,230 --> 00:46:17,970
There's no way you'll make it.

568
00:46:17,970 --> 00:46:19,270
I'll make it back in time.

569
00:46:22,130 --> 00:46:25,530
Don't go. If you guys aren't back in time,

570
00:46:25,530 --> 00:46:27,070
we all get it.

571
00:46:27,070 --> 00:46:30,670
He won't make it because you're too busy playing squad leader. Move.

572
00:46:31,370 --> 00:46:32,370
I said don't go.

573
00:46:32,370 --> 00:46:34,070
You're really gonna push it, huh?

574
00:46:35,600 --> 00:46:36,930
Out of my way, you bastard.

575
00:46:37,730 --> 00:46:39,000
Move.

576
00:46:40,070 --> 00:46:42,030
What's going on, cadets?

577
00:46:42,030 --> 00:46:43,030
Nothing.

578
00:46:43,500 --> 00:46:45,570
I give you a break and you start fighting?

579
00:46:45,570 --> 00:46:47,930
Everyone, fall in. Come on, over here.

580
00:46:48,600 --> 00:46:50,500
Form up. Get in behind. Come in.

581
00:46:50,500 --> 00:46:52,870
Well? Ready yet?

582
00:46:52,870 --> 00:46:54,400
Attention!

583
00:46:54,400 --> 00:46:55,900
Not yet, sir, not yet.

584
00:46:58,970 --> 00:47:00,930
Straighten your uniforms, quickly.

585
00:47:01,530 --> 00:47:02,900
Stand at ease.

586
00:47:05,530 --> 00:47:07,500
We're cadets.

587
00:47:07,500 --> 00:47:09,170
Don't let your emotions run the show.

588
00:47:09,170 --> 00:47:10,770
We have to care about each other.

589
00:47:10,770 --> 00:47:13,270
We live as a unit.

590
00:47:13,270 --> 00:47:15,100
We have to help each other.

591
00:47:15,100 --> 00:47:16,530
We look out for each other.

592
00:47:16,530 --> 00:47:18,400
We're friends.

593
00:47:18,400 --> 00:47:20,970
These small things within our unit —

594
00:47:20,970 --> 00:47:22,700
don't let them divide us.

595
00:47:22,700 --> 00:47:24,830
We have to help each other.

596
00:47:25,970 --> 00:47:29,900
We're friends. These are small things.

597
00:47:29,900 --> 00:47:32,830
Don't hold on to them.

598
00:47:32,830 --> 00:47:40,600
We're here to learn. Don't let this happen again.

599
00:47:44,500 --> 00:47:49,900
Consider this a warning. I hope this doesn't happen again.

600
00:47:50,230 --> 00:47:51,800
Hey, Fuen!

601
00:47:51,800 --> 00:47:53,570
Cadet, come here, come.

602
00:47:53,570 --> 00:47:55,830
Take your friend to the first aid room.

603
00:48:39,870 --> 00:48:41,530
Watch out! It's dangerous!

604
00:48:46,130 --> 00:48:48,000
Hey! Din.

605
00:49:17,300 --> 00:49:18,700
How's Fuen doing?

606
00:49:19,730 --> 00:49:21,030
He's okay now.

607
00:49:23,900 --> 00:49:27,870
Then go take a break. I'll watch Fuen from here.

608
00:49:27,870 --> 00:49:28,970
Thanks a lot.

609
00:49:28,970 --> 00:49:32,670
No. I'm staying until Fuen wakes up.

610
00:49:35,530 --> 00:49:37,100
You like Fuen, don't you?

611
00:49:42,300 --> 00:49:45,970
So what? Do I have to tell you?

612
00:49:47,100 --> 00:49:50,330
You don't have to answer. But you should know this.

613
00:49:53,070 --> 00:49:54,300
Because I like Fuen.

614
00:49:55,370 --> 00:49:56,600
Meaning what?

615
00:49:57,630 --> 00:50:02,100
You mean you're serious, so you're telling me up front?

616
00:50:03,800 --> 00:50:04,770
That's right.

617
00:50:07,870 --> 00:50:09,600
Then do whatever you want.

618
00:50:11,230 --> 00:50:12,870
I don't think you'll win Fuen over anyway.

619
00:50:17,070 --> 00:50:18,000
Really?

620
00:50:19,230 --> 00:50:22,400
That's fine. I'm going after him either way.

621
00:50:23,870 --> 00:50:28,000
Let's play it like this. Fair and square. It's more fun.

622
00:50:44,030 --> 00:50:46,300
"Chemi, you can actually play football?"

623
00:50:46,300 --> 00:50:48,830
"I'm staff, sir."

624
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:54,430
"When you want to win someone over, you should just be yourself."

625
00:50:55,030 --> 00:50:58,970
"There's something I've been wanting to tell you... I like you. Do you have a boyfriend?"

626
00:50:59,900 --> 00:51:01,000
What's wrong with you?

627
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,370
That monkey business is getting to me.

628
00:51:02,370 --> 00:51:03,300
Fuen, here.

629
00:51:03,300 --> 00:51:04,670
Whoa. / Eat up, eat a lot.

630
00:51:04,670 --> 00:51:06,600
Excuse me, I'll go to the bathroom for a bit.

631
00:51:06,600 --> 00:51:07,830
What's up with you today?

632
00:51:07,830 --> 00:51:08,800
You're acting weird.

633
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:11,130
Come to Siam with me. I just wanna be with you.

634
00:51:11,130 --> 00:51:12,130
Humour me, will you?

635
00:51:12,130 --> 00:51:14,400
When I was little, someone promised he'd come after me.

636
00:51:14,400 --> 00:51:15,130
Oh, you mean Aof.

637
00:51:15,130 --> 00:51:15,930
How did you know?

638
00:51:15,930 --> 00:51:17,670
From the way you joined a club you're no good at.

639
00:51:17,670 --> 00:51:20,230
I'm in upper secondary now, and I still don't have anyone.

640
00:51:20,230 --> 00:51:22,230
But Aof still hasn't made a move on me.

641
00:51:22,230 --> 00:51:26,200
This guitar pick— the singer I like uses this brand and this exact finish.

642
00:51:26,200 --> 00:51:27,600
Okay then, I'll buy it for you.

643
00:51:27,600 --> 00:51:29,130
Sir, I'd like to pay.

644
00:51:29,130 --> 00:51:30,030
There you go, kid.

645
00:51:30,030 --> 00:51:31,570
You knew what we were about to do?

646
00:51:33,470 --> 00:51:34,770
That means we didn't do it.

647
00:51:34,770 --> 00:51:37,570
Listen to me. Give it everything. Tear them apart.

648
00:51:37,570 --> 00:51:40,770
I'm surprised you don't know football is a team sport.

649
00:51:40,770 --> 00:51:42,300
Rei, you asshole! / Aof!

650
00:51:42,300 --> 00:51:45,430
He spends too much money. We have to find the funds to support this.

651
00:51:46,300 --> 00:51:49,100
I've said my piece. Because I can definitely do it, Din.

652
00:51:49,100 --> 00:51:51,030
Is the plan I told you about workable?

653
00:51:51,030 --> 00:51:53,000
It's probably way too easy, this staring-into-eyes thing.
